add('jupiter_medicines',283,'the sick felt great comfort','historical_treatment_attribution',['A trine, sextile, OR conjunction occurs between the sixth lord and Jupiter.','Jupiter is in the ninth house.','Moon separates from the sixth lord to Jupiter so placed in the ninth.'],'Lilly calls this an assured argument that medicines prescribed or already taken made the patient very sick while being taken and operating, wrought effectually in outward bodily parts, and afterward brought great comfort and improvement in the parts first afflicted.',uncertainty=['Historical inferential treatment narrative, not a verified clinical example.','The wording does not specify that every kind of discomfort implies effectiveness.'])
